    {
        "content": "<p><span aria-label=\"memo\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f4dd\" role=\"img\" title=\"memo\">:memo:</span> cfallin submitted <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/14237#pullrequestreview-5071079982\">PR review</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Thanks!</p>\n<p>Note that we keep the filetests in the ISA-specific directories as <code>compile</code> tests, so we assert golden assembly-sequence output, and we have runtests in <code>runtests</code> shared among all the platforms. Could you (i) make the test in aarch64 a compile-test, with <code>precise-output</code>, and (ii) find the runtest that tests this in runtests/ and enable it by adding a target line for aarch64?</p>\n</blockquote>",
